  "description": "An attachments group (-C) holds a controller indexed signature group (-K) of three Ed25519 indexed signatures. -K has size 66 (3 x 22 quadlets), not 3; -C has size 67. A digest group follows. This is the framing that made streams unreadable between keripy and the item-counting implementations. The symbol legends of the Encoding Scheme Symbols Table and the indexed-code symbol table say a count code's digits determine 'the count of the following Primitives or groups of Primitives'; this case rests on the explicit rule at the Count Code tables section instead, and the conflict between the two texts is noted, not resolved, here.",
